hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2913","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Abdur-Rahman ibn Mahdi, narrated to us Shu'bah, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Jurayy ibn Kulayb—a man from them—narrate from 'Ali (RA) that the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) forbade sacrificing an animal with a broken horn or ear.\n\nQatadah said: So I mentioned this to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, and he said: \Al-'Adb\"" refers to half or more than half being broken.\n\nNarrated to us Bundar"," narrated to us Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah"," from Sa'id ibn Bashir"," from Qatadah"," from Shahr ibn Hawshab"," who said: \""Al-'Adb\"" refers to a horn that is broken inward.\n\n---"""
